---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro"
import { formatPageTitle } from "@/lib/seo"

const linkClass = "underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-accent"
---

<BaseLayout
  title={formatPageTitle("Accessibility")}
  description="Spoonbowl's accessibility statement: the WCAG 2.2 AA target, what is in place, known gaps and how to report a problem."
  path="/accessibility/"
>
  <div class="wrap py-12">
    <div class="prose-column">
      <header class="mb-8">
        <h1 class="page-title">Accessibility</h1>
        <p class="muted">
          Spoonbowl aims to meet the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2 at level AA.
          This statement was written on <time datetime="2026-11-01">1 November 2026</time>.
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="space-y-8">
        <section aria-labelledby="accessibility-done">
          <h2 id="accessibility-done" class="mb-3 text-lead font-bold">
            What is in place
          </h2>
          <ul class="muted list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
            <li>
              Every page has a skip link to the main content, plus header, navigation, main and
              footer landmarks.
            </li>
            <li>Each page loads as a full document with its own title and one main heading.</li>
            <li>Keyboard focus is always visible.</li>
            <li>
              Search is a combobox you can drive from the keyboard, and it announces the number of
              results to screen readers.
            </li>
            <li>
              Cook mode announces step changes, and its ingredient checklist uses real checkboxes.
            </li>
            <li>Animations are reduced when your system asks for reduced motion.</li>
            <li>The theme follows your system setting, and you can switch to light or dark.</li>
            <li>
              Every <code>.astro</code> file is linted with the strict
              <code>jsx-a11y</code> rules before it ships.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="accessibility-limits">
          <h2 id="accessibility-limits" class="mb-3 text-lead font-bold">
            Known limitations
          </h2>
          <ul class="muted list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
            <li>
              Recipe text and photos come from DummyJSON, which provides no image descriptions.
              Photos next to a recipe name are marked as decorative; elsewhere the alt text is the
              recipe name.
            </li>
            <li>Recipes are only available in English.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="accessibility-report">
          <h2 id="accessibility-report" class="mb-3 text-lead font-bold">
            Reporting a problem
          </h2>
          <p class="muted">
            If something gets in your way, open an issue on
            <a
              href="https://github.com/sg208/spoonbowl/issues"
              class={linkClass}
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >
              GitHub<span class="sr-only"> (opens GitHub issues in a new tab)</span>
            </a>
            . Say which page you were on, what you were trying to do, and your browser and any
            assistive technology you use. Opening an issue needs a free GitHub account.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
